---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/ui/Section.astro";
import SceneWindow from '../components/SceneWindow.astro';
import { pageMetadata } from "../data/metadata";
import { pricingPlans } from "../data/pricingPlans";
import { siteConfig } from "../data/siteConfig";

const minimumTermsText = pricingPlans.map((plan) => `${plan.shortName} has a ${plan.minimumTerm}`).join(". ") + ".";
---

<MainLayout title={pageMetadata.terms.title} description={pageMetadata.terms.description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container page-hero__layout">
      <div class="hero__content">
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p>These Terms explain the general expectations for using the Hometown Boost website and requesting website or local marketing services.</p>
        <p class="note">Last updated: June 4, 2026</p>
      </div>
      <SceneWindow/>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>A signed proposal, invoice, service agreement, or written scope may include additional terms for a specific client project.</p>

      <h2>Services</h2>
      <p>Hometown Boost provides monthly website plans, hosting, maintenance, local visibility support, and optional Google Ads management according to the selected plan and written scope.</p>
      <p>Plan features, update limits, page counts, minimum terms, add-ons, and pricing are described on the Pricing page. If a written proposal or agreement lists a different scope, the written proposal or agreement controls for that client.</p>

      <h2>Pricing, Billing, and Payment</h2>
      <p>Website plans are monthly services with no setup fee. {minimumTermsText}</p>
      <p>Monthly invoices or recurring payments are due according to the invoice or written payment arrangement. If payment is late, Hometown Boost may pause non-urgent updates or support until the account is current. If an account remains unpaid after written notice, hosting or service access may be suspended until payment is resolved.</p>

      <h2>Minimum Terms and Cancellation</h2>
      <p>Clients may request cancellation at any time, but the minimum term for the selected plan still applies. After the minimum term is complete and all outstanding balances are paid, service may continue month to month unless canceled with 30 days' written notice.</p>
      <p>Fees already paid are not refundable unless Hometown Boost agrees otherwise in writing.</p>

      <h2>Client Content and Responsibilities</h2>
      <p>Clients are responsible for providing accurate business information, service details, photos, logos, approvals, access credentials, and other materials needed to complete the work.</p>
      <p>Clients are also responsible for making sure they have the rights to use any text, photos, logos, trademarks, reviews, claims, licenses, or other materials they provide.</p>

      <h2>Website Ownership and Transfer</h2>
      <p>Clients own the business information, logos, photos, written materials, and other content they provide.</p>
      <p>Hometown Boost may use its own systems, processes, design patterns, code libraries, tools, and third-party services to build and maintain websites. Those underlying tools and processes remain the property of Hometown Boost or their respective providers.</p>
      <p>After the minimum term is complete and the account is paid in full, a client may request a static export of the published website content and files where technically practical. Third-party tools, hosting accounts, paid licenses, forms, analytics, automations, and Hometown Boost proprietary systems are not included in a transfer unless agreed in writing.</p>
      <p>Clients are encouraged to own and control their own domain name whenever possible. If Hometown Boost helps with domain setup, domain access and renewal responsibilities should be documented in writing.</p>

      <h2>Google Ads Management</h2>
      <p>Google Ads management is optional. Advertising spend is separate from Hometown Boost management fees and is paid directly to Google by the client unless otherwise agreed in writing.</p>
      <p>Hometown Boost does not guarantee ad results, cost per lead, lead volume, revenue, rankings, or any specific business outcome.</p>

      <h2>No Guaranteed Results</h2>
      <p>Hometown Boost works to improve the client's website foundation, presentation, local visibility, and lead paths. Results depend on many factors outside Hometown Boost's control, including market demand, competition, budget, reviews, pricing, follow-up speed, seasonality, and customer behavior.</p>
      <p>Hometown Boost does not guarantee search rankings, lead volume, sales, revenue, ad performance, or business outcomes.</p>

      <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>Websites, forms, hosting, analytics, advertising, email, domains, maps, fonts, plugins, and other tools may rely on third-party providers. Hometown Boost is not responsible for outages, policy changes, pricing changes, or service interruptions caused by third-party providers.</p>

      <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>To the fullest extent allowed by law, Hometown Boost will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or lost-profit damages related to use of this website or services.</p>

      <h2>Updates to These Terms</h2>
      <p>These Terms may be updated from time to time. The updated version will be posted on this page with a revised Last updated date.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these Terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</MainLayout>
